\par
\b Quota History CSV Sample\b0\par
The quota history snapshot captures current quota usage. Key fields:\par
- CapturedAtUtc/Local: Timestamp of the snapshot\par
- SubscriptionName: Which subscription's quota\par
- Region: Azure region (centralus, eastus, etc.)\par
- QuotaName: Quota family name (standardBsv2Family, cores, etc.)\par
- CurrentValue: Current usage\par
- Limit: Quota limit\par
- Available: Limit minus CurrentValue\par
\par
Example row: ME-MngEnvMCAP374870-jeffpigott-1, centralus, standardBsv2Family, 0 current, 200 limit, 200 available\par
\par
\b Quota Group Candidates CSV Sample\b0\par
The candidates report identifies quota families with surplus capacity. Example shows:\par
- 1856 total candidates across 2 subscriptions\par
- Top candidates by suggested movable amount: standardBsv2Family (180), standardDSv4Family (180), standardDv2Family (96)\par
- CandidateStatus field shows "Candidate" when surplus is available\par
- SuggestedMovable shows recommended amount to return to group quota pool\par
\par
\b Quota Group Discovery Results\b0\par
When -QuotaGroupDiscover is specified with -QuotaGroupManagementGroupId Demo-MG:\par
- Discovered quota groups: 1\par
- ManagementGroupId: Demo-MG\par
- GroupQuotaName: standardbstesting\par
- DisplayName: Standard BS Testing\par
- GroupType: AllocationGroup\par
- ProvisioningState: Succeeded\par
\par
\b Interpreting Results\b0\par
Candidates Report Interpretation:\par
- High SuggestedMovable values (100+) indicate significant surplus capacity\par
- Multiple candidates per family across subscriptions show potential for consolidation\par
- Total candidates count (1856 in example) shows scope for consolidation\par
\par
Next Steps After Capture:\par
1. Review the CSV files to understand current quota distribution\par
2. Use -QuotaGroupPlan to generate a move plan\par
3. Apply with -QuotaGroupApply to execute the moves\par
4. Monitor with -CaptureQuotaHistory in scheduled tasks over time\par
\par
\b Flowchart (text)\b0\par
Hourly capture -> Discover groups -> Select group/region/family -> Read allocation -> Build target -> PATCH update -> Poll request status -> Read-after-write verify -> Record success\par
